%I A394955 #24 Aug 12 2026 00:14:21
%S A394955 1,1,7,178,12717,2274106,965053751,946082787574,2106916436350137,
%T A394955 10522377595446828082,116585611748768997632955,
%U A394955 2839494560108245988977500286,150827018838560668532015603263061,17354894736600039325810662254201073322
%N A394955 Number of reducible flow graphs on n labeled nodes whose entry node 1 is a global source (in-degree 0, reaches every node).
%C A394955 The distinguished-entry version is 2^(n-1)*a(n) for n >= 2 (edges into the entry are free); self-loops multiply by 2^(n-1) (none on the source).
%C A394955 Computed by the same SCC-region recurrence as A398465.
%D A394955 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A394955 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A394955 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A394955 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A394955 a(n) = A398465(n)/2^(n-1).
%o A394955 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[1] # See Python link in A398465 for program code.
%Y A394955 Cf. A398465, A350792 (all single-source digraphs).
%K A394955 nonn
%O A394955 1,3
%A A394955 _Gregory Morse_, Aug 05 2026
